{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>For it was not specified what should be done to him.</b> Rashi: in what manner of execution he shall die. And if you ask: let them judge him by strangulation, for every death penalty stated generically in the Torah is by strangulation — one may answer: Moses was uncertain whether we derive חלול חלול (desecration) from idolatry, so that he would be executed by the sword. Therefore they placed him in custody. And if you ask: according to Rabbi Yehudah, who says he is not executed unless they inform him at the time of warning in which manner of execution he will be killed — how could they have judged him to death? One may answer: perhaps they warned him regarding all four modes of execution, and he accepted upon himself death by all of them."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:18:08.906847791Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}